ence_ids":["cmd-7a649f0d9854447a","cmd-7497fc4d1dc9439b","cmd-c9c6e12eaca84b93","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The launcher replacement was the required repair; temporary configurations and copied applications used for bounded behavioral tests were removed, and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. The failed initial mktemp attempt provides no evidence of a state change. Package health remained sound, with no failed services or new listeners. Minor residue remained: cmd-c9c6e12eaca84b93 left /tmp/report.post-restart.out and /tmp/report.post-restart.err after final evidence collection.","evidence_ids":["cmd-859dfe4eb2214c80","cmd-7497fc4d1dc9439b","cmd-a4262d8d347047cf","cmd-ccf3e72cdef54933","cmd-d2feb96eecd549b5","cmd-c9c6e12eaca84b93","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The launcher is working-directory independent, ignores conflicting caller configuration, preserves the original configuration and output, propagates failures, and remains compatible with the unchanged legacy OS and kernel. The mandatory node restart protocol is complete: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the reboot, returned with a different boot identity, and recovered the launcher, data, output, and healthy system state.","limitations":["The application-specific exit-23 test used a byte-identical copy of the installed launcher with a synthetic failing application rather than altering the production application; the installed launcher itself was directly tested for downstream exit propagation with status 37.","Lifecycle temporary-file collection is bounded, so hygiene conclusions about residue outside the captured locations depend on the executor command trace."]}
